<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!--
        REMOVED: view_hospital_patient_list_receptionist_no_create (priority 32,
        groups_id=[receptionist]) and view_hospital_patient_list_manager_create_override
        (priority 40, groups_id=[manager, admin]).

        They hid the "New" button on the Patients list from receptionists while
        layering a higher-priority override to give it back to managers and
        admins, who hold the Receptionist group implicitly.

        The pair is invalid AND inoperative on Odoo 18:

          * ir.ui.view._check_groups rejects groups_id on any view that has an
            inherit_id and mode != 'primary', which is what aborted the upgrade.

          * Even without that constraint the mechanism no longer works.
            _get_inheriting_views selects extension views on `active` and
            mode='extension' ONLY (it does not filter by groups_id at all),
            so both views would be combined into one arch for every user and
            the priority-40 create="1" would simply win for everybody.

        It cannot be re-expressed with node-level groups="..." either, which is
        what the constraint's message recommends. That works on ELEMENTS: the
        combined arch keeps the attribute and _postprocess drops nodes the user
        cannot see. Here the restriction is a ROOT ATTRIBUTE applied through
        <xpath position="attributes">, and attribute specs are consumed during
        inheritance (odoo/tools/template_inheritance.py handles no groups) so
        they never survive to be filtered per user.

        Nothing is lost from the security boundary. The authoritative control
        always was, and remains, _assert_can_create_directly() in
        models/hospital_patient.py: it blocks direct creation by a receptionist
        on every path including raw RPC, and it is unaffected by what any view
        shows. A receptionist now sees the New button and gets that method's
        explicit "use the reception workflow" error; managers and admins keep
        the button working exactly as before.

        Restoring the nudge per role needs a bridge-owned action carrying
        context={'create': False} behind a group-restricted menu, because the
        patient menus belong to hospital_management, which this module does not
        edit.
    -->

</odoo>
